    "q-69856": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69856",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251486/assets/3247a3ba0e4434860318ef697e29f7d377cfb0eb08135bb5d3e147516b2a5505.png)\n\nConsider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{CD},$ shown above. Which of the following could be $\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC}?$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ to the head of $\\overset{\\to }{DC}.$ Therefore, we obtain a new vector for which the tail and head is the same point, the tail of $\\overset{\\to }{CD}.$ \n\nThat vector is called the zero vector, and we write\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC}=0.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251486/assets/8e51db7c2e9eff46679a185b82a477d65842d43d1dd71289f3e6bab1a7a503de.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-69856-a",
              "type": "image",
              "value": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251486/assets/44c890a2ab9f5c3ed67deecee95c76bc663010e3331da48c14d9504c242aeb2a.png",
              "html": "<img src=\"/graphics/q-69856-a-5\">",
              "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-69856-a-5",
              "source_urls": [
                "https://mathacademy.com/graphics/q-69856-a-5"
              ]
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
